From 979152b7d94ffe1cf1b1bcdb5b24adff74323065 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Oct 2025 17:55:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 612/913] core: arm: pageable PM sequences (extend to
 PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND)

Allow Arm PM sequence for 32bit machines to be almost fully pageable,
relaxing the pressure on the secure internal RAM, more specifically on
the physical pages pool of the pager. The feature is under configuration
switches CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF, CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND,
CFG_PAGED_PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND.

The PSCI fastcall SMC already reach smc_std_handler() and
tee_psci_handler() functions. These 2 are modified to pass a new
argument that is the PSCI function to be called in a pageable context,
and then both return a status on whether the PSCI service was executed
(SM_EXIT_TO_NON_SECURE) or the PSCI service is to be executed in a
thread and pageable context (SM_EXIT_TO_PM_THREAD).

When a thread/pageable PSCI handler is to be called, secure monitor
exists to secure world through new vector_thread_pm_entry() with PSCI
handler function arguments in thread_smc_args::r0..r5 and handler
entry address in argument thread_smc_args::r6.
In turn vector_thread_pm_entry() calls thread_handle_pm() to allocate
the thread. Function thread_handle_pm() may return with an error
status if no thread context is available. Because the PM sequences are
expected to be uninterruptible, flag THREAD_FLAGS_NATIVE_INTR_DISABLE
is define for OP-TEE native (secure) interrupts to be masked in the
pageable PM thread context.

Generic 32bit PM helper function sm_pm_cpu_do_suspend() and
sm_pm_cpu_do_resume() are changed to save and restore the FIQ, abort
and undefined exception contexts and are declared unpaged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git bbda33c257a937b88561b9db1310ef5d19c56108 core: arm: pageable PM sequences (extend to PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND)]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ibd9972a9eae8353a7444128c02348bb3f41e9c24
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/501263
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/sm/psci.c  |  9 +++++++++
 core/include/keep.h      | 10 ++++++----
 core/include/kernel/pm.h |  3 ++-
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/sm/psci.c b/core/arch/arm/sm/psci.c
index 520ad8692..b9ec8de61 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/sm/psci.c
+++ b/core/arch/arm/sm/psci.c
@@ -162,6 +162,15 @@ uint32_t tee_psci_handler(struct thread_smc_args *args,
 		args->a0 = psci_version();
 		break;
 	case PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND:
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CFG_PAGED_PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND)) {
+			args->a0 = a1;
+			args->a1 = a2;
+			args->a2 = a3;
+			args->a3 = (vaddr_t)nsec;
+			*thread_pm_handler = (vaddr_t)psci_cpu_suspend;
+
+			return SM_EXIT_TO_PM_THREAD;
+		}
 		args->a0 = psci_cpu_suspend(a1, a2, a3, nsec);
 		break;
 	case PSCI_CPU_OFF:
diff --git a/core/include/keep.h b/core/include/keep.h
index 126a50e2c..cbad996c4 100644
--- a/core/include/keep.h
+++ b/core/include/keep.h
@@ -46,11 +46,13 @@
 #endif /* __ASSEMBLER__ */
 
 /*
- * DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM() makes resource unpaged unless both of
- * CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND and CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF
- * are enabled.
+ * DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM() makes resource unpaged unless
+ * CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND, CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF and
+ * CFG_PAGED_PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND are enabled.
  */
-#if defined(CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND) && defined(CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF)
+#if defined(CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND) && \
+    defined(CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_OFF) && \
+    defined(CFG_PAGED_PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND)
 #define DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM(sym)	static int __unused sym##__LINE__
 #else
 #define DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER_PM(sym)	DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER(sym)
diff --git a/core/include/kernel/pm.h b/core/include/kernel/pm.h
index 29c64b26e..9022dacb2 100644
--- a/core/include/kernel/pm.h
+++ b/core/include/kernel/pm.h
@@ -95,7 +95,8 @@ typedef TEE_Result (*pm_callback)(enum pm_op op, uint32_t pm_hint,
  * Callback implementations should ensure their functions belong to unpaged
  * memory sections (see DECLARE_KEEP_PAGER()) since the callback is likely to
  * be called from an unpaged execution context unless
- * CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND and CFG_PAGED_SYSTEM_OFF are enabled.
+ * CFG_PAGED_PSCI_SYSTEM_SUSPEND, CFG_PAGED_SYSTEM_OFF and
+ * CFG_PAGED_PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND are enabled.
  *
  * Power Mamagement callback functions API:
  *
